Z||000000||Black88GT||02-14-2001||05:06 PM||||I have some parts I would like to get powder coated.  I thought everything was hunky dory and I would just pick the closest shop to do it, until I went to this site talking about how important it is to have a good person doing it, and how they can screw it up if not properly done. <P>So, anyone here have any recommendations?  Right now I just need an upper plenum/exhaust crossover done but soon I will need much more.  Shipping is not bigdeal if I am guaranteed it will get done right...<P><BR>TIA<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||stimpy||02-14-2001||05:24 PM||||Air-Borne Coatings here in Oahoma City did my plenum and valve covers. It's been over a year since they were done at a cost of $120 and they still look brand new. They can do just about any color under the sun including an aluminized finish that looks just like the Jet-hot. Their phone # is 405-685-4433. ||||reg||1
